module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.BaseSites
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.SubcategorySite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ChangeOfSites.ChosenEtalePrecoverage
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Topos.MorphismOfTopoi

/-!
# Stacks 07AK for either of its two topologies at once

Stacks 07AK fixes `τ` to be either the étale or the fppf topology and asks the full subcategory
`𝒳' ⊆ 𝒳` to be closed under the morphisms of `𝒳` lying over a *smooth* (in the étale case)
respectively a *flat and locally finitely presented* (in the fppf case) morphism of schemes. The
closure condition and the choice of topology are therefore not independent: they are the two
halves of a single alternative, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.IsClosedUnderSitePullback` packages as a disjunction over the
`AlgebraicGeometry.SiteKind` selector of Stacks 06TP.

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/SubcategorySite.lean` proves continuity and cocontinuity of
the inclusion for a general topology `τ` on the underlying category of schemes and a general
closure property `Q`, and instantiates that at the fppf topology and at any chosen étale
precoverage. This file assembles those two instantiations into the single statement quantified
over `AlgebraicGeometry.SiteKind` with the closure condition packaged, which is the form the
source states: the hypothesis pins `τ` down to one of the two admissible values and hands over
exactly the closure property belonging to it.

Note that the étale case needs the chosen étale precoverage of Stacks 03FF to be named, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.etalePrecoverage`; the two descriptions of the big étale topology — the one
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.baseTopology` selects at `AlgebraicGeometry.SiteKind.etale` and the
one generated by that precoverage — agree definitionally.

Full faithfulness, the third of the three properties the source asserts of the inclusion, is
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.fullyFaithfulι`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.IsClosedUnderSitePullback`: the two alternative closure conditions of
  Stacks 07AK (1), packaged as a disjunction over the topology selector.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.inclusionToposMorphism`: the morphism of topoi the inclusion defines.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback`:
  continuity and cocontinuity of the inclusion of the full subcategory, for either of the two
  topologies the source admits.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.inclusionToposMorphism_inverseImageIso`: the inverse image of that
  morphism of topoi is ordinary restriction, which is Stacks 00XR (1) at this inclusion.

The remaining assertion of the source — that restriction identifies the cohomology of the
subcategory site with that of the ambient one — is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.subsiteCohomologyIsoOfAtlas`, and the whole of Stacks 07AK is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.subsite_cohomology_comparison`, both in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/SubsiteCohomologyAtlas.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07AK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07AK)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

/-! The inclusion of a full subcategory is fully faithful with no hypothesis at all, so the first
assertion Stacks 07AK makes about the inclusion is Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.fullyFaithfulι` itself. -/

universe u v w

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  {X : Type v} [Category.{w} X] (p : X ⥤ BigFppfOver B S hS) (P : ObjectProperty X)

/-- **The closure condition of Stacks 07AK (1).** A full subcategory of `𝒳` is closed under the
pullbacks relevant to the topology `τ` when either `τ` is the étale topology and the subcategory
is closed under the morphisms of `𝒳` lying over a smooth morphism of schemes, or `τ` is the fppf
topology and it is closed under those lying over a flat, locally finitely presented one.

The disjunction is what ties the closure property to the topology, and it is also what restricts
`τ`: of the five topologies of Stacks 06TP only the étale and the fppf one admit this
condition. -/
def IsClosedUnderSitePullback (τ : SiteKind) : Prop :=
  (τ = .etale ∧ ∀ {x y : X} (f : x ⟶ y),
      Smooth (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x) ∨
  (τ = .fppf ∧ ∀ {x y : X} (f : x ⟶ y),
      Flat (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) →
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation (B.inclusion.map (p.map f).left) → P y → P x)

/-- **Continuity of the inclusion in Stacks 07AK.** Let `p : 𝒳 ⥤ (Sch/S)` be a category fibred
in groupoids over the big fppf category of a scheme `S` in `B`, let `τ` be the étale or the fppf
topology of Stacks 06TP, and let `P` cut out a full subcategory closed under the pullbacks `τ`
calls for. Then the inclusion of the full subcategory is continuous for the topology it inherits
(Stacks 06NV).

The étale half is the instantiation of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_etaleTopology` at the chosen étale precoverage of
Stacks 03FF, the fppf half is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_fppfTopology`, and the hypothesis chooses between
them. -/
theorem isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback (τ : SiteKind)
    (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (hclose : IsClosedUnderSitePullback B S hS p P τ) :
    P.ι.IsContinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
      (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ) := by
  rcases hclose with ⟨rfl, h⟩ | ⟨rfl, h⟩
  · exact isContinuous_ι_etaleTopology B S hS p (etalePrecoverage B)
      (map_mem_schemeEtalePrecoverage_of_mem_etalePrecoverage B) hp P
      @h
  · exact isContinuous_ι_fppfTopology B S hS p hp P @h

/-- **Cocontinuity of the inclusion in Stacks 07AK.** Under the hypotheses of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback` the
inclusion of the full subcategory is also cocontinuous. -/
theorem isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback (τ : SiteKind)
    (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (hclose : IsClosedUnderSitePullback B S hS p P τ) :
    P.ι.IsCocontinuous (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
      (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ) := by
  rcases hclose with ⟨rfl, h⟩ | ⟨rfl, h⟩
  · exact isCocontinuous_ι_etaleTopology B S hS p (etalePrecoverage B)
      (map_mem_schemeEtalePrecoverage_of_mem_etalePrecoverage B) hp P
      @h
  · exact isCocontinuous_ι_fppfTopology B S hS p hp P @h

/-- **Stacks 07AK, the morphism of topoi.** Cocontinuity of the inclusion gives the adjoint pair
`g^{-1} ⊣ g_*` between the topos of the subcategory site and that of the ambient site, with
`g^{-1}` left exact: the morphism of topoi `g : Sh(𝒳'_τ) ⟶ Sh(𝒳_τ)` of the source.

The sheaves take values in `Type max v w`, which is the universe in which the sheaves of sets on
either site live. -/
@[stacks 07AK "the morphism of topoi `g : Sh(𝒳'_τ) ⟶ Sh(𝒳_τ)` defined by the inclusion, \
whose inverse image is restriction to `𝒳'`"]
def inclusionToposMorphism (τ : SiteKind) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hclose : IsClosedUnderSitePullback B S hS p P τ) :
    MorphismOfTopoi
      (Sheaf (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
        (Type max v w))
      (Sheaf (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ) (Type max v w)) := by
  letI := isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback B S hS p P τ hp hclose
  exact {
    pushforward := P.ι.sheafPushforwardCocontinuous (Type max v w)
      (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
      (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ)
    inverseImage := P.ι.sheafPullbackCocontinuous (Type max v w)
      (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
      (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ)
    adj := P.ι.sheafAdjunctionPullbackCocontinuous (Type max v w)
      (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
      (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ)
    preservesFiniteLimits := by infer_instance }

/-- **The inverse image in Stacks 07AK is restriction.** Because the inclusion is both continuous
and cocontinuous, the sheafification in `g^{-1}G = (ι^p G)^#` is unnecessary and `g^{-1}` is
ordinary restriction along `ι`, so `g^{-1}G(x) = G(x)`. This is Stacks 00XR (1), here
`CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafPullbackCocontinuousIsoSheafPushforwardContinuous`, at this
inclusion.

The source's remaining assertion — that `H^p(𝒳'_τ, g^{-1}F) = H^p(𝒳_τ, F)` for every abelian
sheaf `F` — is `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.subsiteCohomologyIsoOfAtlas`. -/
def inclusionToposMorphism_inverseImageIso (τ : SiteKind) (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hclose : IsClosedUnderSitePullback B S hS p P τ) :
    letI : P.ι.IsContinuous
        (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
        (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ) :=
      isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback B S hS p P τ hp hclose
    (inclusionToposMorphism B S hS p P τ hp hclose).inverseImage ≅
      P.ι.sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type max v w)
        (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
        (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ) := by
  letI := isContinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback B S hS p P τ hp hclose
  letI := isCocontinuous_ι_associatedTopology_of_isClosedUnderSitePullback B S hS p P τ hp hclose
  exact P.ι.sheafPullbackCocontinuousIsoSheafPushforwardContinuous (Type max v w)
    (P.ι.inheritedTopology (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ))
    (BigFppfOver.associatedTopology B S hS p τ)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

end
